0,Sámi music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sámi_music,"Their music incorporated Sámi elements such as yoik singing, Sámi lyrics, and shamanic drum. The vocalist has also yoiked for fellow Finnish folk metal band Finntroll.","Saami, Ter",Uralic
1,Ter Sámi - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ter_Sámi,"Ter Sámi is the easternmost of the Sámi languages. It was traditionally spoken in the northeastern part of the Kola Peninsula, but now it is a moribund language; in 2004, only ten speakers were left.","Saami, Ter",Uralic
2,Sámi languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sámi_languages,"The Sámi languages form a branch of the Uralic language family. According to the traditional view, Sámi is within the Uralic family most closely related to the Finnic languages (Sammallahti 1998).","Saami, Ter",Uralic
3,Sami Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL8E83C3FC9FEBD879,"The Sami are the native peoples of northern Norway, Sweden, Finland, and Russia. This playlist features several Sami musicians, such as Mari Boine, Sofia Jannok, Adjagas, and more.","Saami, Ter",Uralic
4,Sámi Music – 30 Indigenous Voices and Living Joik Traditions,https://www.muzeap.com/sami-music/,"Feb 22, 2026 · Discover Sámi music through a curated listening journey that honors vocal traditions, drum practices, and Arctic cultural heritage.","Saami, Ter",Uralic
5,Music - M.A. Castrénin seura - ugri.net,https://www.ugri.net/in-english/cultures/saami-peoples/music/,"In addition to traditional music, features from Saami culture and Saami languages are strongly alive in modern music, too. In the 1990s, Saami music was made known by Angelin tytöt (Aŋŋel nieiddat), a group with a strong vocal line.","Saami, Ter",Uralic
6,Sámi musihkka - Music in Sami languages - Rate Your Music,https://rateyourmusic.com/list/kyvetti/sami_musihkka___music_in_sami_languages/,"Sep 29, 2025 · Most common traditional musical style of Sami is Joik (Yoik, Juoiggus, Juoigan, Luohti). It is a singing style reflecting specific people or places, traditionally sung a cappella or accompanied by drum, though several modern singers perform with a wide variety of instruments and fusion styles.","Saami, Ter",Uralic
7,"Saami, Ter | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/sjt/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..7gEynVXqWzhIuR7bMEz32cvOPUQJtsM-Qo-H9kW3q-I,Ter Saami is an endangered indigenous language of the Russian Federation. It belongs to the Uralic language family.,"Saami, Ter",Uralic
8,Ter Saami Research Papers - Academia.edu,https://www.academia.edu/Documents/in/Ter_Saami,"Ter Saami is a Uralic language spoken by the Ter Saami people in the Kola Peninsula of Russia. It is a critically endangered language, part of the Sámi language group, and is characterized by its unique phonetic and grammatical features, reflecting the cultural heritage of the Saami community.","Saami, Ter",Uralic
9,Saamic,https://copius.univie.ac.at/etymology/slides_06_saamic.pdf,"Saamic. Community of Practice in Uralic Studies (COPIUS) Foundations of Uralic etymology www.copius.org.Areal variation of the Saami languages in a historical context. Nine living languages: Southern, Ume, Pite, Lule, Northern, Inari, Skolt, Kildin, Ter Saami.","Saami, Ter",Uralic
